 "marker_source_togglefilter", "label": "toggleFilter(type, btn) \u2014 toggles feedback-type highlight filter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "marker_source_toggletheme", "label": "toggleTheme() \u2014 toggles dark/light mode", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "marker_source_calib", "label": "CALIB \u2014 marking calibration prompt fragment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encodes anti-inflation AND anti-compression marking policy: state-wide score distributions are given as context only (not a quota), best-fit banding is mandated, and a consistency check reconciles criterion ratings with the holistic score \u2014 designed to make the AI mark like a real VCAA assessor rather than a lenient or overly cautious one."}, {"id": "marker_source_examctx", "label": "EXAMCTX \u2014 exam context prompt fragment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Grounds the AI's judgement in real exam constraints (3-hour handwritten exam, ~55-60 minutes per section) so it does not penalise exam-appropriate length or expect take-home polish."}, {"id": "marker_source_report_a", "label": "REPORT_A \u2014 Section A assessor-report calibration text", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encodes 2024-2025 VCAA assessor report guidance for Section A (text response) so the AI rewards/penalises the same features real assessors flagged, rather than generic essay-marking heuristics."}, {"id": "marker_source_report_b", "label": "REPORT_B \u2014 Section B assessor-report calibration text", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encodes 2024-2025 VCAA assessor report guidance for Section B (creating texts) to calibrate marking to real assessor-identified strengths and weaknesses."}, {"id": "marker_source_report_c", "label": "REPORT_C \u2014 Section C assessor-report calibration text", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encodes a skill-ladder (LOW to HIGH) drawn from VCAA assessor reports for Section C (argument analysis), explicitly to reward strategic selection and audience-effect analysis over technique-checklisting."}, {"id": "marker_source_cinstr", "label": "CINSTR \u2014 inline comment output-format instructions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "marker_source_precision_mode", "label": "Precision mode (3x independent marking, median reported)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trade-off deliberately chosen: marks three times independently and reports the median \u2014 slower but more reliable than a single pass, and the mark spread across the three passes flags borderline scripts for human review."}, {"id": "marker_source_second_opinion_feature", "label": "Second opinion \u2014 blind re-mark (moderation feature)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "marker-source.html", "source_location": null, "